{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"a4806b8c33684b39","type":"text","text":"After taking over Cilindrath the unhileg fought amongst each other for hundreds of years in a power struggle until one lich of power far beyond any living creature to ever exist known only as the Whispered one began taking control of each faction within the Unhileg. Eventually The Whispered one Lorded over the entire continent with an iron fist and all on the continent were forced to either do his bidding or become his undead slave. Many tried to beseech him of his throne but all failed.\n\n1800 P.D\n\nOne day Vecna grew board and began to gain memories of a lost magic from nearly a thousand years ago. With memories of this power in his mind he began to lust for power and hunger to become that of a God and so a God he became and any who dare question him were condemned to eternal suffering as an undead servant. \n\nWord began to spread across the sea to the new found nation known as the Volstarian Dynasty and the Askain Empire. After learning of The whispered one the two nations denied his God hood and bestowed him the title of the False God. \n\nNobody knows his name but whispers drift through history of his evil nature and lust for power. \n\nThe whispered one grew more and more angry at the nations abroad and began to create a city that could soar through the skies for the next 100 years. \n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nShortly after receiving word of an ancient artifact from the Draemont family the false God was approached by a man named Verazanoth who told him that he should seek the power out for himself and that it could truly turn him into the God he wanted so badly to become. \n\nSo The whispered one and his armies invaded Askain in an attempt to steal The Dreamers Heart from them. During the invasion the Caesars wife and child were in Askain visiting the beaches and were kiled in the invasion. \n\nThe attempted invasion was stopped midway through by Caesar he killed the False God claiming his revenge and abandoning his title as a king.\n\nAfter slaying The Whispered one Caesar banished his right hand man to the shadow fell to rot in a barren horror filled land for eternity.\n\nAfter the battle both Azest and The Dreamers Heart along with her were lost ","x":-125,"y":-30,"width":1085,"height":750},
		{"id":"3c182232cc98c58c","type":"text","text":"[[The Rise of The Whispered one.canvas]]\n[[Unhileg.canvas]]\n[[Verazanoth.canvas]]\n[[The Whispered One.canvas]]\n[[Divina Cilindrath.canvas]]\n#Lore ","x":-216,"y":-270,"width":436,"height":170}
